# The unzipped Foundry release — redistributable binaries, and large.
# Re-download from https://foundryvtt.com/me/licenses instead of committing.
app/

# User data: worlds, systems, modules, assets, Logs.
# Never commit this. Two reasons beyond size:
#   1. Config/options.json and Config/license.json hold your license key.
#   2. Worlds and compendia are LevelDB directories — binary, unmergeable,
#      and they corrupt under git's line-ending handling.
# To version-control campaign content, use the Foundry CLI to unpack
# compendia to YAML/JSON first (see README.md).
data/
